kers are often branded as a nutritious and convenient way to consume a staple food or cereal grain."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-cracker"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cracker_(food)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":6,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Strawberry delight","dish/strawberry-delight"]]],["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]],["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Canapé","dish/canape"]]],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Canapé","dish/canape"]]],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Whipped cream","ingredient/whipped-cream"],["Paste","ingredient/paste"],["Puff pastry","ingredient/puff-pastry"],["Spread","ingredient/spread"],["Toast","ingredient/toast"],["Carabao mango","ingredient/carabao-mango"],["Condensed milk","ingredient/condensed-milk"],["Graham crackers","ingredient/graham-crackers"],["Ladyfinger (biscuit)","ingredient/ladyfinger-biscuit"],["Mango","ingredient/mango"],["Savoiarde PAT","ingredient/savoiarde-pat"],["Cream cheese","ingredient/cream-cheese"],["Gelatin","ingredient/gelatin"],["Gelatine dessert","ingredient/gelatine-dessert"],["Graham cracker","ingredient/graham-cracker"]]}]},"ingredient/shallot":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/shallot","n":"Shallot","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 17 dishes across 8 cuisines","intro":[["The shallot ( or ) is a cultivar group of the onion. Until 2010, the (French red) shallot was classified as a separate species, Allium ascalonicum. The taxon was synonymized with Allium cepa (the common onion) in 2010, as the difference was too small to justify a separate speci